g config.local_to_jira_link equals the link-type components of RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK), so the lock-step criterion has a covering step.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC5: 'a parity test keeps config.local_to_jira_link in lock-step with RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK's link-type components'","Testing section enumerates only test_link_config_effect, test_link_skip_preserved, test_link_undeclared_fails_closed","Approach step 1 says local_to_jira_link is 'parity-tested like local_to_jira_status' but no test step names it"],"finding":"AC5 requires a parity test keeping config.local_to_jira_link in lock-step with RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK's link-type components, but the Testing section lists only three tests (test_link_config_effect, test_link_skip_preserved, test_link_undeclared_fails_closed), none of which is the parity test.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9333c2bdf86a6023","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (final bullet) vs Testing section","norm_id":"nfd5e62cc3670c453","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future edit to RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK diverges from local_to_jira_link with no test catching it"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a named test (e.g. test_local_to_jira_link_parity) that asserts {k: v[0] for k, v in RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK.items()} == config.local_to_jira_link.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how config-aware REMOVE attribution recovers BLOCKING DIRECTION when the blocking link_type is overridden, given the reverse map `{v:k ...}` is non-injective (blocks and depends_on share one vendor type); either scope out overriding the Blocks type, or key the fallback on the (type, swap) pair / defer to direction like resolve_inbound_link.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3112,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK (value_maps.py:104): blocks->(Blocks,False), depends_on->(Blocks,True) — two relations, one vendor type; direction lives in the swap flag","link_direction.py:20 JIRA_LINK_TO_RELATION={'Blocks':'blocks','Relates':'relates_to'} recovers only the outward base, then INVERSE_RELATION flips it by inward/outward — a flat str->str reverse cannot reproduce this","Plan: 'the built-in reverse map stays the direction-aware first attempt' acknowledges direction matters but does not state the config fallback loses it"],"finding":"The config-aware REMOVE reverse map `{v: k for k, v in link_map.items() if v != SKIP}` is non-injective: blocks and depends_on both map to the SAME vendor type ('Blocks' in the built-in literal), because direction is carried by the built-in `swap` flag, not the link_type. The fallback `reverse.get(opaque_vendor_type)` therefore collapses to an arbitrary (dict last-writer) relation. This is masked for the built-in 'Blocks' (JIRA_LINK_TO_RELATION resolves it direction-aware, so the fallback isn't reached), but if an operator overrides the blocking link_type (blocks/depends_on -> a custom vendor type), the remote type is unknown to the built-in reverse, hits the collapsed fallback, and REMOVE attribution can pick the WRONG blocking relation — mis-comparing against local_deps/managed_refs.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdde471b9dde408b0","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3, REMOVE bullet: 'Build reverse = {v: k for k, v in link_map.items() if v != SKIP}'","norm_id":"nc4b37b4ce185a150","priority":0.2888,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator sets [mapping] link_map blocks = 'DCBlocks' (a renamed blocking type); a managed, locally-absent remote 'DCBlocks' link reverses via the collapsed map to depends_on instead of blocks, so (relation, local_target) misses local_deps/managed_refs and the REMOVE is mis-gated"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Note in step 3 that the reverse fallback is only sound for symmetric relations (relates_to) and TYPE-renamed non-blocking links; for the blocking pair, either explicitly declare overriding the Blocks link_type out of scope for S4, or recover direction from the remote link's inward/outward side (as resolve_inbound_link does) before consulting the config reverse.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium